// endpoint_fork_session.proto — ForkSession: make this shim's conversation a
// fork of another, cut at a fork point, BEFORE any session starts.
//
// THE VENDOR WRITES THE FORK. The shim calls the vendor's own session fork,
// which copies the parent's records with their content unchanged — so the
// fork's first request reads the parent's whole prefix from the prompt cache —
// gives the copy a new vendor session id, and stamps every copied record with
// the parent record it came from. The shim then files the new transcript under
// its own working directory, where a resume of the new id finds it.
//
// SEPARATE FROM StartSession. The daemon persists the fork's vendor session id
// before it starts the session, so a start refused as cold, or one that fails
// and is retried, resumes the SAME fork rather than forking again.
//
// THE FORK'S BOOK IS ITS OWN. The copied records are the parent's, already
// filed in the parent's book; the file plane skips them by their stamp, so the
// fork's book holds only what the fork itself goes on to say. A reader of the
// fork reads its inherited past from the parent's book, which this answer names.
//
// THE PARENT'S TRANSCRIPT MUST BE UNDER THIS SHIM'S ACCOUNT ROOT: the vendor
// reads it from the root its caller runs under. A parent filed under another
// account is refused as `unknown_session`.

